================================================================================
TEST 20358 -- Loopback between two ports on same switch
================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-09 19:14:22-19:17:37 NZDT (tb470 time; the x230 holds NZ wall time labelled
          UTC, ~2 s behind tb470; the stack clock is true UTC)
Bench:    tb470, consoles u0 (x230, DUT), u5 (stack master); Test Engineer terrenceb@terrenceb-dl
Tester:   bench-runner (by hand: tools/tb ckcon -> tools/ckcon.py with its @poll / @sleep
          directives, tools/tb qmark -> tools/qmark.py, tools/rcdiff.py, tools/rc2cfg.py; no
          framework script)
Graded:   tester
Case:     AWPTCM-T20358 (Approved), objective "When a switch port receives its own BPDU from the
          same edge port, it sets the port to the blocking state. When it no longer receives
          BPDUs, it sets the port to the forwarding state.", 1 step
Build:    swi_f awplus_main-20261008-57 (x230v2_28GS-awplus_main-20261008-57.rel), bootloader 6.2.40
          stk_a awplus_main-20261008-57, members 1/3/4
Configs:  swi_f.cfg (running-config with the case setup, `spanning-tree rstp enable`), stk_a.cfg
          (running-config before the stack's one change); saved to startup: no

VERDICT: PARTIAL -- the case could not be run: the bench's only candidate "hub/switch", the
         IE520 stack with spanning tree disabled, did not return the x230's own BPDUs, so no
         loop could be closed safely and the Backup/Discarding check was never reached
      RSTP enabled on the x230 ........................ done  (Spanning Tree Enabled, x230 root)
      stack bridges the two x230 links (VLAN 103) ..... done  (stack port1.0.3 + port1.0.17)
      x230 port1.0.4 receives its own BPDU ............ NO    ("Received None", Designated
                                                               Forwarding for 20 s)
      loop, broadcast traffic, Backup/Discarding, no TX on the backup port ... NOT RUN
NOT RUN: STEP 1, bullets 2-5 (create the loop, send broadcast traffic, confirm the port is Backup
         / Discarding, confirm the backup port does not transmit). With the stack bridging its two
         x230 links, x230 port1.0.4 received no BPDU in 20 s (10 hello intervals) and stayed
         Designated Forwarding, so closing the data loop (x230 port1.0.4 into VLAN 103) would have
         made a loop with no blocking port. The stack offers no setting that passes BPDUs: the
         only `no spanning-tree rstp enable` option is `bridge-forward`, the interface
         `spanning-tree` options hold nothing that tunnels BPDUs, and `l2 ?` is "% Unrecognized
         command".
UNBLOCK: give the x230 a BPDU-transparent loop between two of its own ports. Move the AT-SPSX
         from stack port3.0.7 (free) into x230 port1.0.6 and the AT-SPSX from stack port4.0.7
         (free) into x230 port1.0.7, then patch one multimode LC-LC lead x230 port1.0.6 <->
         port1.0.7 (or cable two x230 ports into a hub). Then the case runs as: RSTP on the x230,
         port1.0.6 and 1.0.7 in one VLAN -> port1.0.7 Backup / Discarding; tb470 eth3 (x230
         port1.0.5, moved into that VLAN) sends the broadcast, and port1.0.7's transmit counter
         stays flat.
CAVEAT:  the case's "IXIA" is replaced by a host NIC on this bench; none of the case's expected
         result ("Backup port should not forward any packet in this state") was measured.

